  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Emergency Health Response in the Winter Affected Hard-To-Reach Areas in Afghanistan</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Building on existing IOM Migration Health programming and in coordination with the Health Cluster, this project includes 1) The provision of primary health care including reproductive and child health care services, nutrition, COVID-19 vaccination as well as mental health and psychosocial support services through 4 temporary static Health Sub Centers and 6 Mobile Health Teams and 2) Health education and health promotion on prevention, and mitigation measures for respiratory infections and other winter-related risks through 4 Community Mobilizer Teams. This project targets the most underserved localities in high prioritized districts in two provinces (Badakhshan and Takhar).</narrative>
  </description>
